# Workshop repo — house rules for any AI agent working in this codebase

## Where things live

- Agents are in `agents/*.md` (the `agents/` folder at the repo root).
- Skills are in `skills/*.md`.
- Specs are in `docs/specs/*.md`.

When you need to invoke an agent or skill, read the file in `agents/` or `skills/` directly. Do not duplicate the content into a Cursor-specific file — the whole point of this repo is that these are portable.

## Code style

- TypeScript everywhere. `strict: true`.
- NestJS follows standard Nest conventions (module per feature, controller + service split).
- Angular uses standalone components and the new control-flow syntax (`@if`, `@for`).
- No new dependencies without a reason — call it out if you add one.

## When writing or modifying code

- Read nearby files first. Match their patterns.
- Prefer editing to adding. If a utility exists, use it.
- If the exercise doc says "don't touch X," don't touch X.
